        "original_id": "5d98d3b1-9e89-5e8e-80db-48a21ff74b09",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Franz Schreker, Luigi Cherubini, Ludwig van Beethoven\n- Works: Irrelohe, Médée\n- Roles: Composer, conductor, teacher, administrator\n- Places: Monaco, Berlin, France\n\nFacts:\n- Luigi Cherubini was born in September 1760 and died on 15 March 1842.\n- Luigi Cherubini was an Italian composer who spent most of his working life in France.\n- Ludwig van Beethoven regarded Luigi Cherubini as the greatest of his contemporaries.\n- Franz Schreker was born on 23 March 1878 in Monaco and died on 21 March 1934 in Berlin.\n- Franz Schreker, originally named Schrecker, was an Austrian composer, conductor, teacher, and administrator.\n- Médée is a French-language opéra-comique by Luigi Cherubini.\n- Irrelohe is an opera in three acts by Franz Schreker, and Franz Schreker also wrote its libretto.",
